## Executes the macro calls of the content edited with a WYSIWYG editor whose content syntax is not HTML (e.g.
## BlockNote), so that the editor can show the output of the macro calls that were inserted or modified, by the current
## user or by the other users editing the same content in realtime. All the macro calls are executed because the output
## of a macro call can depend on the rest of the content.
##
## The request has to be sent to the document where the edited content is saved, which is the context of the macro
## calls, and it takes the following parameters:
## * content: the edited content, in the syntax of the editor
## * editorSyntax: the syntax of the editor (e.g. blocknote/1.0), used to parse the edited content and to render the
##   result, which is sent back as plain text
## * sourceSyntax: the syntax used to save the edited content (e.g. xwiki/2.1); defaults to the syntax of the document
## * restricted: "true" to execute the macros in a restricted context (e.g. when editing a comment)
## * form_token: the CSRF token
## * collaboration: the realtime collaboration session where the content is edited, if any; the content is then
##   executed with the rights of the session participant with the least script rights among those that changed the
##   content, instead of the rights of the current user
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#if ($request.method != 'POST' || !$services.csrf.isTokenValid($request.form_token))
